cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ShapeComplexity in your research, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "ShapeComplexity: entropy-based metrics for quantifying edge- and macro-shape complexity"
abstract: >-
  ShapeComplexity is a high-performance Rust tool for quantifying the shape
  complexity of leaves and other biological structures from PNG images. It
  decomposes a shape into complementary edge and macro-shape layers, converts
  each into a signal curve, and quantifies edge complexity (EC) via approximate
  entropy and macro-shape complexity (MC) via spectral entropy. It also reports
  fractal dimension, circularity, shape index and area. Command-line and
  graphical interfaces are provided.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-26
license: MIT
